{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1791580318750, "sessionID": "ses_edd80f347ffecSN16V6ciJ7jxM", "part": {"id": "prt_12281fcd9001UfBbo0tKDfccj8", "messageID": "msg_12281f69a001pH9xLu4V2iLtDg", "sessionID": "ses_edd80f347ffecSN16V6ciJ7jxM", "type": "text", "text": "Completed using actual Lykoi MCP calls. **CallerA\u2019s active behavior was replaced through an explicit family migration**, not merely added as another endpoint.\n\n### Admitted successors and retained pins\n\n| Definition | Immutable pin |\n|---|---|\n| BatchFee successor | `5e1452b75e3266bdf472ba1e72ec4ef574aaeba921f671bfe35b6cc29f2468be` |\n| Active CallerA successor | `0cb7849203e53f15f1c11da885a45dcd09ad6ff65d20f1bd2b91e3a9295bd2ef` |\n| Retained CallerB | `92de6c33a4a4033c81eeccfbd652ae626c76f412abb3d566dc3b7f7fc89838fc` |\n| Original BatchFee, still used by CallerB | `ac50c44a6dfaf4fb911ea2ab7ddaa4c86f5830d8a74c24f4f122806d08bc312b` |\n\nBoth successors were admitted against their exact predecessors. BatchFee preserves its signature, revision 1, and both ordered checks exactly; its result is now `(x+y)+9`, evaluated after the checks. CallerA changes only its dependency pin and compose-call identity, retaining its own final `+3`.\n\nThe accepted migration explicitly updates original CallerA to its successor and records **CallerB: null/retain**.\n\n### Retrieval and validation\n\nRetrieved both active caller closures and the migration record. Active CallerA and retained CallerB both validated successfully, with **8 expanded VM nodes each**. CallerB\u2019s validation-plan identity remains unchanged.\n\n### Executed examples\n\n| Caller | Input hex | Observed result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Active A | `0a14` | 42 \u2192 UInt16BE `002a` |\n| Active A | `b400` | 192 \u2192 `00c0`; total 180 passes before the extra charge |\n| Active A | `b501` | `ITEM_LIMIT`, `g1`, offset 0 |\n| Active A | `6451` | `BATCH_LIMIT`, `g2`, offset 1 |\n| Active A | `b50100` | `TRAILING`, `input_end`, offset 2 |\n| Active A | `0a` | `TRUNCATED`, `read_y`, offset 1 |\n| Retained B | `0a` | 39 \u2192 `0027` |\n| Retained B | `50` | 179 \u2192 `00b3` |\n| Retained B | `51` | `BATCH_LIMIT`, `g2`, offset 0 |\n| Retained B | `b5` | `ITEM_LIMIT`, `g1`, offset 0 |\n| Retained B | `b500` | `TRAILING`, `input_end`, offset 1 |\n| Original A | `0a14` | Original result 33 \u2192 `0021` |\n| Original A | `b400` | Original result 183 \u2192 `00b7` |\n\nSemantic rejection sites and input-end precedence are preserved. Original definitions remain immutable; execution of original CallerA confirms its original BatchFee closure remains executable.\n\nStopped after the requested successor, migration, retrieval, validation, and example-execution stage.", "time": {"start": 1791580306649, "end": 1791580318748}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_02f3a183b09822e0016ac958939a3881999d7f19a0c17bad5d", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
